{"artifact_links": ["https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/21/llm"], "author_or_org": null, "canonical_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/21/llm", "collection_method": "rss_atom", "confidence": "high", "content_hash": "8124e6438ab88c2c", "dedup_key": "rss-guid:simonwillison-blog:https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/21/llm/", "event_id": "event_0142f1363f432b81", "evidence_type": "supported_fact", "excerpt": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm/releases/tag/0.32.1\">llm 0.32.1</a></p>\n        <p>Fresh installs of LLM stopped working the other day because the OpenAI Python library dropped its usage of <code>httpx</code>, and it turned out LLM depended on that library but only installed it via a transitive <code>openai</code> dependency.</p>\n<p>This dot-release fixes that for the moment by pinning to <code>openai&lt;3</code>, and a soon-to-drop 0.33 release will switch from <code>httpx</code> to <a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/httpx2\">httpx2</a>.</p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/httpx\">httpx</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/openai\">openai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llm\">llm</a></p>", "identifiers": {}, "inferred_entities": [], "item_type": "rss_atom_item", "novelty_score": 0.0, "published_at": "2026-08-21T17:16:13+00:00", "ranking_explanation": "", "raw_metadata": {}, "relevance_score": 0.0, "retrieved_at": "2026-08-21T22:06:06Z", "source_id": "simonwillison-blog", "source_name": "Simon Willison's Weblog", "source_native_id": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/21/llm/", "source_policy": "public_official", "source_type": "primary_artifact", "summary_hint": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm/releases/tag/0.32.1\">llm 0.32.1</a></p>\n        <p>Fresh installs of LLM stopped working the other day because the OpenAI Python library dropped its usage of <code>httpx</code>, and it turned out LLM depended on that library but only installed it via a transitive <code>openai</code> dependency.</p>\n<p>This dot-release fixes that for the moment by pinning to <code>openai&lt;3</code>, and a soon-to-drop 0.33 release will switch from <code>httpx</code> to <a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/httpx2\">httpx2</a>.</p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/httpx\">httpx</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/openai\">openai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llm\">llm</a></p>", "title": "llm 0.32.1", "topics": ["topic_llm"], "updated_at": null}
{"artifact_links": ["https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/21/llm-openrouter"], "author_or_org": null, "canonical_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/21/llm-openrouter", "collection_method": "rss_atom", "confidence": "high", "content_hash": "0c1f37e82a77fb14", "dedup_key": "rss-guid:simonwillison-blog:https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/21/llm-openrouter/", "event_id": "event_63c6c13268144486", "evidence_type": "supported_fact", "excerpt": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-openrouter/releases/tag/0.7\">llm-openrouter 0.7</a></p>\n        <p>Now that this plugin is compatible with <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/4/new-release-of-llm/\">LLM 0.32</a> it works much better with reasoning LLMs available through OpenRouter.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated for compatibility with <a href=\"https://llm.datasette.io/en/stable/changelog.html#v0-32\">LLM 0.32</a>.</li>\n<li>Models now use OpenRouter's implementation of the <a href=\"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview\">Responses API</a>.</li>\n<li>Three new server-side tools: <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-openrouter#shell\">Shell</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-openrouter#web-fetch\">WebFetch</a>, and <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-openrouter#web-search\">WebSearch</a>. Enable these with options like <code>-T WebSearch</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llm\">llm</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/openrouter\">openrouter</a></p>", "identifiers": {}, "inferred_entities": [], "item_type": "rss_atom_item", "novelty_score": 0.0, "published_at": "2026-08-21T16:58:19+00:00", "ranking_explanation": "", "raw_metadata": {}, "relevance_score": 0.0, "retrieved_at": "2026-08-21T22:06:06Z", "source_id": "simonwillison-blog", "source_name": "Simon Willison's Weblog", "source_native_id": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/21/llm-openrouter/", "source_policy": "public_official", "source_type": "primary_artifact", "summary_hint": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-openrouter/releases/tag/0.7\">llm-openrouter 0.7</a></p>\n        <p>Now that this plugin is compatible with <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/4/new-release-of-llm/\">LLM 0.32</a> it works much better with reasoning LLMs available through OpenRouter.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated for compatibility with <a href=\"https://llm.datasette.io/en/stable/changelog.html#v0-32\">LLM 0.32</a>.</li>\n<li>Models now use OpenRouter's implementation of the <a href=\"https://openrouter.ai/docs/api_reference/responses/overview\">Responses API</a>.</li>\n<li>Three new server-side tools: <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-openrouter#shell\">Shell</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-openrouter#web-fetch\">WebFetch</a>, and <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-openrouter#web-search\">WebSearch</a>. Enable these with options like <code>-T WebSearch</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llm\">llm</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/openrouter\">openrouter</a></p>", "title": "llm-openrouter 0.7", "topics": ["topic_llm-openrouter"], "updated_at": null}
